<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 11 and below (`android:fullBackupContent`). The Android 12+ twin is
  `data_extraction_rules.xml`; both must be kept in step, because a device on
  either side of that line reads only its own file.

  Progress photos are the only thing excluded, and the reason is that the
  consent sheet makes a promise about them. `photosConsentOnDevice` says
  "there is no copy on a server" and `photosConsentNoBackup` says "there is no
  backup ... nobody can restore them for you". Auto Backup is on by default and
  covers the whole app data directory, so without this file both sentences were
  false: the encrypted `.bin` envelopes would ride to the user's Google Drive.

  `app_flutter` is not a name we chose. `getApplicationDocumentsDirectory()` on
  Android resolves to `PathUtils.getDataDirectory()`, which is
  `context.getDir("flutter", MODE_PRIVATE)`, and `getDir` prefixes `app_`. It
  sits directly under the app data root, which is what `domain="root"` means
  here - `domain="file"` is `getFilesDir()` and would miss it entirely.

  The Flutter `SharedPreferences` file IS excluded (privacy decision B). It
  holds `profile.sensitive.<uid>` and `profile.sensitive.corrupt.<uid>`
  (plaintext health/injury data), the per-account training-context answer and
  the legacy `progress_photos.key.v1` AES key. Backup rules exclude files, not
  keys, so the whole file goes: the cost is that locale/theme/notification
  settings are not restored either, and on a new device the user is asked the
  profile and training-context questions again. Flutter's `shared_preferences`
  on Android stores everything in `FlutterSharedPreferences.xml`
  (`domain="sharedpref"` is `shared_prefs/`).

  The `flutter_secure_storage` preference files are excluded too:
  `FlutterSecureStorage.xml` (values) and `FlutterSecureKeyStorage.xml`
  (wrapped cipher keys). Wrapped keys restored without the original Keystore
  entry cannot be unwrapped, so they must not travel.

  The activity journal (S02-02, GPS-PRIV-083) is excluded as well:
  `activity_journal` (the production per-account tree
  `<support>/activity_journal/<scopeId>`; excluding the directory excludes every
  scope beneath it) plus the legacy `journal`, `sources` and `quarantine`, all
  directly under `getFilesDir()` (the app support directory,
  `domain="file"`). They hold routes, heart rate and laps; the
  stream key lives in the excluded secure-storage files, so a restored copy
  would be undecryptable anyway. The names come from `journal_layout.dart`
  (`kActivityBackupExcludedDirs`); keep both files and that constant in step.

  Everything else in the app stays backed up. This is an exclusion list, not a
  switch: `android:allowBackup` is untouched.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="root" path="app_flutter/progress_photos" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSharedPreferences.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSecureStorage.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSecureKeyStorage.xml" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="journal" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="sources" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="quarantine" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="activity_journal" />
</full-backup-content>
